  "root_cause_assessment": "Same library bytes and allocator remove the between-build identity/layout confound for this cohort. Endpoint recycle drops from about 170 ns to 77 ns, but acquisition rises 75 to 91 ns. Profile queue wait is 4.51 vs 4.63 us and response handoff 3.94 vs 3.65 us. Mixed profiles include seed and metrics and overlap; no additive CPU attribution. These observations and the timed regressions defeat response-object replacement as a sufficient solution. Scheduling/parking contention is a plausible remaining cause, not uniquely proved.",
